# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenBolt shell completion
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This file is generated by `bolt completion <shell>`; do not edit it.
# Edit the completion model, hints and templates instead.
#
# Installation:
#   bash: source the generated file from ~/.bashrc or install it in your
#         bash-completion completions directory as `bolt`.
#   zsh:  source the generated file from ~/.zshrc, or install it as `_bolt`
#         in a directory in $fpath and restart the shell.
#
# Dynamic completions call `bolt plan show`, `bolt task show`, `bolt group
# show` and `bolt inventory show` (with `--format json`) for plan, task and
# target names, and `bolt plan/task show <name>` for parameter names. Results
# are cached in memory for the shell session, keyed by project (the --project
# argument or the current directory) and the newest mtime among the project's
# definition files, so entries refresh automatically when the project changes.
# Everything falls back to plain message completions when `bolt` is not on the
# PATH.
#
# Optional configuration (set in the shell before completing):
#   BOLT_COMPLETION_TARGETS  individual targets are offered for --targets/-t,
#                            not just groups; set to 0, "false", "off" or "no"
#                            to disable (useful for large inventories)
#   BOLT_COMPLETION_RUBY     ruby to use when jq is unavailable
#                            (default: /opt/puppetlabs/bolt/bin/ruby, bolt's
#                            bundled all-in-one interpreter; falls back to the
#                            system ruby)
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
